<title>JAPAN: Japan jobless rate rises to 3.3 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Japan jobless rate rises to 3.3 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate rose to 3.3 percent in April, up from 3.2 percent in March, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The jobs-to-applicants ratio for April was 0.71, down from 0.73 the previous month, the Labour Ministry announced separately. This means there were 71 job openings for every 100 job seekers.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			    April     March     Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		   3.3 pct   3.2 pct   3.4 pct</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	  0.71	0.73	0.67</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			  April     March     Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		   3.4 pct   3.5 pct   3.5 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed		2.31 million  2.34 million  2.35 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		  April	year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				 65.74 million  +1.2 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p> Manufacturing			 14.47 million  +2.3 pct</p>
<p> Services				16.52 million  +2.7 pct</p>
<p> Wholesale, retail, restaurants  14.85 million  +1.7 pct</p>
<p> Construction			   6.71 million  +0.1 pct</p>
<p> Agriculture			    3.46 million  -2.3 pct</p>
</text>
